    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the aesthetics thing, but i've been watching them. they don't just move them around for decoration. every time they do maintenance, the placement is so precise it feels like they're calibrating something. \n\nplus, monstra leaves are broad and stiff, right? and snake plants are upright and narrow. if you were trying to create a focal point for sound waves to bounce off into a central collector, wouldn't that specific mix of broad surfaces and vertical baffles actually work for directing noise from the study areas toward the corners? it's not just about dampening, it's about how the sound travels through the room.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
